# ---------------- SelfTest.events (Task 51 Part C) ----------------
# The project's self-test sheet: ordinary events that drive the game and assert what happened,
# so a mechanic's play-check is one run that prints PASS/FAIL/SKIP per case and a count, instead
# of "open the editor, hold W, and look".
#
# SETUP (editor) — `Content/scenes/SelfTest.scene` is the authored scene:
#   1. Player: a CharacterController with an EventSheet whose Event File is `SelfTest`, standing
#      on the Floor. Tick "Use Physics Movement" and "Configure Character Body"; the sheet reads
#      `me is on ground` through the controller's own probe. "Self Test" is ticked too (the
#      filename convention would mark it anyway).
#   2. Props, all empty actors (positions in the scene): StartPad, JumpPad, Marker, TouchPad,
#      WatchPoint, FarAway, LadderFoot, Ladder, CheckpointA, SpawnPoint, BreakPoint, Dummy and
#      Breakable (both with a BoxCollider — Dummy's is solid so `me sees` can ray-cast to it,
#      Breakable's is a trigger). `SelfTest_Coin` is an inactive template for `spawn`.
#   3. ResultLabel in a UICanvas: the bind at the bottom shows the two counters, so the answer is
#      readable in-game as well as in the console.
#   4. One EventsManager on GameManager, as every scene needs.
#
# THE WORDS — four of them, and a case is a block:
#   test "<label>"   names the case; without it the case is `case 1`, `case 2`, … by block order.
#   expect <condition>  asserts any condition the language already accepts (`is`, `is not`,
#                    `higher than`, `near`, `exists`, `does not exist`, `has tag`, …). It is
#                    parsed by Conditions.Parse, so there is no second comparison grammar.
#   pass             closes the case as passed. A case without `pass` still passes when its body
#                    runs to the end — `pass` is how a reader sees the case end.
#   when self test ends   one summary hook, raised once after every case has settled.
# A false `expect` fails the case, prints the expectation's own text, and keeps running the body
# (so the chain below still reaches the later cases). A case whose gate never opens is SKIP, never
# PASS. `self test timeout <n> seconds` raises the 5 s deadline; a stuck case quotes its last line.
#
# WHY THE MESSAGES: every case must run one at a time, and a case is a block, not a sequencer. The
# first case opens on `me appears`; each case ends by sending the next case's message to itself, so
# the blocks read top to bottom and a wait in one case can never overlap the next. Cases tagged
# "(editor only)" need real physics/ray-casts and are the documented editor tier (Task 51 Part D);
# everything else also runs in the headless suite against the fake world.
#
# `expect count of …` (Task 28) is not in the language yet, so the first sheet has no case for it.

# --- the counter the timer case reads --------------------------------------
when every 0.25 seconds
  add 1 to my Ticks

# =========================================================================
# CASE 1 — variables and set/add
# =========================================================================
when me appears
  test "variables and set/add"
  self test timeout 8 seconds
  set my Count to 2
  add 1 to my Count
  expect my Count is 3
  pass
  send message "case 2" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 2 — timers and wait
# =========================================================================
when message "case 2" arrives
  test "timers and wait"
  set my Ticks to 0
  wait 0.7 seconds
  expect my Ticks is higher than 1
  pass
  send message "case 3" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 3 — variables and edges: `becomes` fires on the edge, not every tick
# =========================================================================
when my Count becomes 3
  add 1 to my EdgeHits

when message "case 3" arrives
  test "an edge fires once, not per tick"
  set my EdgeHits to 0
  # 3 → 4 crosses nothing; 4 → 3 is the one equality edge. (`becomes 3` also fires on a
  # downward crossing of 3, so 3 → 1 → 3 would honestly count twice.)
  set my Count to 4
  wait 0.2 seconds
  add -1 to my Count
  wait 0.5 seconds
  expect my EdgeHits is 1
  pass
  send message "case 4" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 4 — movement and `goto` arrival
# =========================================================================
when me arrives at Marker
  set my Arrived to 1

when message "case 4" arrives
  test "goto arrives at the marker"
  teleport me to StartPad
  wait 0.3 seconds
  set my Arrived to 0
  set my Speed to 400
  goto Marker
  wait 1.4 seconds
  # `me is near Marker` would only see actors that carry a sheet (FindNamedActor), and a
  # waypoint has none — the arrival edge itself is the assertion that works in both tiers.
  expect my Arrived is 1
  pass
  send message "case 5" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 5 — `send message` routing: the dummy's own sheet answers
# =========================================================================
when message "case 5" arrives
  test "message routes to the dummy"
  set PingCount to 0
  send message "ping" to Dummy
  wait 0.3 seconds
  expect PingCount is 1
  pass
  send message "case 6" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 6 — contact is enter-edge, not per-tick
# =========================================================================
when me touches TouchPad
  add 1 to my TouchCount

when message "case 6" arrives
  test "contact is enter-edge (editor only)"
  set my TouchCount to 0
  teleport me to TouchPad
  wait 0.8 seconds
  expect my TouchCount is 1
  teleport me to StartPad
  wait 0.3 seconds
  pass
  send message "case 7" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 7 — `sees` / `stops seeing` edges
# =========================================================================
when me sees Dummy by 900
  set my Seen to 1

when me stops seeing Dummy
  set my LostSight to 1

when message "case 7" arrives
  test "sees then stops seeing (editor only)"
  teleport me to FarAway
  wait 0.5 seconds
  set my Seen to 0
  set my LostSight to 0
  teleport me to WatchPoint
  wait 0.6 seconds
  expect my Seen is 1
  teleport me to FarAway
  wait 0.6 seconds
  expect my LostSight is 1
  pass
  send message "case 8" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 8 — jump: take-off, then landing (the airborne gate also refuses a double jump)
# =========================================================================
when message "case 8" arrives
  test "jump takes off and lands (editor only)"
  teleport me to JumpPad
  wait 0.5 seconds
  expect me is on ground
  jump strength 420
  wait 0.15 seconds
  expect me is airborne
  wait 1.5 seconds
  expect me is on ground
  pass
  send message "case 9" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 9 — ladder: `climb` holds the ascent, then the climb ends and the body lands
# The 40 cm "do not re-grab at the top" gate is the sheet's own condition, documented in
# Platformer.events; the language has no "is not near", so that edge stays a visual check.
# =========================================================================
when message "case 9" arrives
  test "ladder climb starts and lands (editor only)"
  teleport me to LadderFoot
  wait 0.4 seconds
  climb Ladder
  wait 0.4 seconds
  expect me is climbing
  wait 2 seconds
  expect me is on ground
  pass
  send message "case 10" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 10 — `save checkpoint` on touch, and the `CheckpointSaved` gate that makes it once
# =========================================================================
when me touches CheckpointA
  my CheckpointSaved is 0
  save checkpoint
  set my CheckpointSaved to 1
  add 1 to my SaveCount

when message "case 10" arrives
  test "checkpoint saves on touch (editor only)"
  set my CheckpointSaved to 0
  set my SaveCount to 0
  teleport me to CheckpointA
  wait 0.8 seconds
  expect my CheckpointSaved is 1
  expect my SaveCount is 1
  teleport me to StartPad
  wait 0.3 seconds
  teleport me to CheckpointA
  wait 0.6 seconds
  expect my SaveCount is 1
  pass
  send message "case 11" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 11 — `respawn at` returns the body to the marker
# =========================================================================
when message "case 11" arrives
  test "respawn at returns to the marker (editor only)"
  teleport me to FarAway
  wait 0.4 seconds
  set my Speed to 400
  goto Marker
  wait 0.3 seconds
  respawn at CheckpointA
  wait 0.4 seconds
  expect me is near CheckpointA by 80
  expect me is on ground
  pass
  send message "case 12" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 12 — `spawn` clones the template and its own sheet runs
# =========================================================================
when message "case 12" arrives
  test "spawn runs the clone sheet (editor only)"
  set CoinSpawned to 0
  spawn SelfTest_Coin at SpawnPoint
  wait 0.8 seconds
  expect CoinSpawned is 1
  pass
  send message "case 13" to me

# =========================================================================
# CASE 13 — `destroy` removes the prop (`does not exist` is the readable half)
# =========================================================================
when me touches Breakable
  destroy Breakable

when message "case 13" arrives
  test "destroy removes the prop (editor only)"
  teleport me to BreakPoint
  wait 0.5 seconds
  expect Breakable does not exist
  pass

# =========================================================================
# the summary hook: one line after every case has settled
# =========================================================================
when self test ends
  print "Self test finished: the PASS/FAIL/SKIP lines above are the report."

# The counts, live on screen as well as in the console.
bind ResultLabel to TestPassed and TestFailed format "Self test — PASS {0} / FAIL {1}"
